  fanchan aggregate 22.218 -> 127.542 B/cycle over 1 -> 64 readers (x5.74)
  onechan aggregate 22.214 -> 22.102 B/cycle over 1 -> 64 readers (x0.99)
  VERDICT: ENDPOINT BOUND -- the fan-out control scaled x5.74 while the
  same readers on ONE channel managed only x0.99, which is 17% of it.
  Same reader count, same issue loop, same transaction size: only the
  endpoint differed, so the endpoint is what cost the difference. This is
  the shape tt-sim's DramChannels term asserts. It is CORROBORATION and
  never provenance: it cannot make dram.bandwidth chargeable, least of all
  on a part with no published DRAM page.
  samecore: not run on this part, so a channel limit and the limit of the
  one router link every onechan flow converges on stay confounded.
